Carafe: a framed game window whose outer rectangle already fills the screen keeps its place. Its client origin
is only the frame's thickness inside a window placed at (0,0), so subtracting it would push the frame off the
screen. This holds when Restore clears the maximized style before the geometry changes; a smaller or offset
window, or a captionless fullscreen one, still follows the existing path.
LGPL-2.1-or-later, as the file it changes.

--- a/dlls/win32u/winnx_drv.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/winnx_drv.c
@@ -906,6 +906,11 @@
     height = client.bottom - client.top;
     screen_width = get_system_metrics( SM_CXSCREEN );
     screen_height = get_system_metrics( SM_CYSCREEN );
+    if ((get_window_long( game, GWL_STYLE ) & WS_CAPTION) == WS_CAPTION &&
+        get_window_rect( game, &window, dpi ) &&
+        !window.left && !window.top &&
+        window.right == screen_width && window.bottom == screen_height)
+        return;
     if (width != screen_width || height != screen_height)
     {
         ret = wine_nx_fit_screen( width, height );
